in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @magic
in @frame
in @cyberpunk

# @smarts/epistemologic — the cybernetic-property-altitude adapter
# species. Bridges @smarts (substrate-architectural integration; #83)
# with @epistemologic/cybernetic (declarative cybernetic property family;
# cybernetic foundation 2026-06-09) honestly via the adapter pattern,
# following the @smarts/{pack, magic, frame, cyberpunk} precedents.
#
# Tick 61 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 60's residue:
# @smarts/cyberpunk landed at e5b682f (recursion-lock-tower altitude;
# fourth cross-family adapter). The family-root forward-promise set
# continues:
#
#   adapters: magic ✓  pack ✓  frame ✓  cyberpunk ✓  epistemologic ← THIS  kintsugi
#
# === The recognition this species realizes (with honest hedge) ===
#
# @smarts.smarts records carry `cybernetic_extra: ref` as the fifth
# form field (per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4 closure). The typed-field
# is BARE ref, not a typed record — because @epistemologic/cybernetic
# is a property-FAMILY, not a single typed substrate, so the field's
# substrate-pull-correct shape is "declarative-property-bundle" with
# species-altitude refinement.
#
# This adapter EXPOSES the field projection + acknowledges the
# substrate-architectural fact that the cybernetic discipline has NO
# single family-root bilateral predicate. Each cybernetic property
# species (@epistemologic/cybernetic/variety, /eigenform,
# /good_regulator, /viable, /autopoiesis, /distinction, /conversation,
# /coevolution, /bateson_learning, /algedonic, /second_order) exports
# its OWN bilateral; consumer species name the SPECIFIC cybernetic
# property they assert.
#
# === The adapter pattern (modified per substrate-architectural fact) ===
#
# The other @smarts/<family> adapters discharge a single family-root
# bilateral (discipline_flexible + <family-root-predicate>). This
# adapter:
#
#   - Projects the cybernetic_extra field (single typed lift)
#   - Lifts a typed cybernetic property to @smarts integration
#     (single typed lift; opaque ref because the property is parametric)
#   - Declares smarts_satisfies_epistemologic_cybernetic bilateral that
#     discharges discipline_flexible alone at the smarts altitude. The
#     consumer species name the SPECIFIC cybernetic property bilateral
#     (e.g., variety_holds, eigenform_fixed) in their OWN requires
#     clauses; this adapter does not pretend to discharge cybernetic
#     property-checking from a family-root predicate that doesn't exist.
#
# Substrate-pull-honest framing: the cybernetic property discipline IS
# parametric over the eleven canonical properties; the @smarts
# integration's cybernetic_extra field carries the property-bundle;
# the bilateral check fires at the SPECIFIC property the consumer
# names. The substrate-decl reflects this structural fact.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994.
#   functor adjunction          Mac Lane 1971.
#   cybernetic foundation       systemic.engineering f9e0402 (1,659
#                               lines, 2026-06-09); the canonical doc
#                               for the 11-property family.
#   Ashby Cybernetics           Ashby 1956. The foundational substrate
#                               ancestor of the declarative cybernetic
#                               property discipline.
#   Beer VSM                    Beer 1972, 1979. The viable-system
#                               5-function audit; one of the 11
#                               canonical properties.
#   eigenform                   von Foerster 1981; Kauffman 2003. The
#                               fixed-point identity discipline
#                               (recognition #38).
#   knowledge commons           Ostrom 1990.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT pretend a single family-root bilateral exists at
#    @epistemologic/cybernetic. The substrate is honest about the
#    property-family structure.
# 2. Does NOT discharge specific cybernetic property checks (variety,
#    eigenform, etc.). Consumer species name those directly.
# 3. Does NOT absorb @epistemologic/cybernetic into @smarts.
# 4. Does NOT replace the @smarts/cyberpunk adapter's recursion-lock-
#    tower discipline. @cyberpunk integrates cybernetic properties
#    OPERATIONALLY at the tower altitude; @epistemologic/cybernetic
#    is the DECLARATIVE property family the operational tower
#    inherits from.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at cybernetic-property-altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole adapter (honest): smarts_satisfies_epistemologic_
# cybernetic returns SATISFIED when the @smarts integration's
# discipline-flexibility holds AND consumer species name specific
# cybernetic property bilaterals that discharge substantively.
#
# Narcissus-pole adapter (deceptive): claims SATISFIED via vocabulary-
# only verification — the cybernetic_extra field is populated but
# consumer species don't name specific property bilaterals. The
# substrate is structurally honest about this gap by NOT including a
# single bilateral that pretends to discharge cybernetic property
# discipline from family-root altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror,
#               shards/epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]]
#                       (the 11-property family this adapter
#                       acknowledges as substrate-architectural fact),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (the cybernetic_extra
#                       field IS bare ref because @epistemologic/
#                       cybernetic is a property-family; the bare-ref
#                       is substrate-architecturally honest).
# Related shards: smarts.mirror, epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror,
#                 smarts/{pack, magic, frame, cyberpunk}.mirror
#                 (sibling cross-family adapters; this adapter is
#                 substrate-architecturally distinct due to
#                 @epistemologic/cybernetic's property-family
#                 structure).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/smarts/epistemologic.mirror` declares
# `@smarts/epistemologic` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/mathematics/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/cybernetics/ashby-1956
source @arxiv/cybernetics/beer-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981
source @arxiv/common-goods/ostrom-1990

prism @smarts/epistemologic {
  focus epistemologic
  project epistemologic
  split epistemologic
  shift epistemologic
  settle epistemologic
}

# === epistemologic_cybernetic_form_of adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action projecting the cybernetic
# property bundle from a @smarts integration. The smarts.cybernetic_
# extra field IS the cybernetic property bundle at substrate-decl
# altitude (bare ref because the property-family is parametric).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the projection itself
# is field access at substrate-decl altitude.
epistemologic_cybernetic_form_of(s: smarts) -> ref { \ }

# === epistemologic_cybernetic_as_smarts adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a cybernetic property
# bundle to a @smarts integration with the cybernetic_extra field
# populated. Other smarts fields populated as default refs.
#
# Round-trip identity at the cybernetic_extra altitude:
#   epistemologic_cybernetic_form_of(
#     epistemologic_cybernetic_as_smarts(cb)
#   ) = cb
# for all cybernetic property bundles cb.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
epistemologic_cybernetic_as_smarts(cb: ref) -> smarts { \ }

# === smarts_satisfies_epistemologic_cybernetic bilateral predicate ===
#
# The cross-family bilateral predicate in @smarts at the cybernetic-
# property altitude. The substrate-pull-honest discharge:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) (@smarts family-root): discharges
#      that the @smarts integration maintains substrate-architectural
#      discipline-flexibility under perturbation.
#
# UNLIKE the other @smarts/<family> adapters: NO SECOND requires
# clause discharging a family-root predicate at
# @epistemologic/cybernetic, because no single family-root predicate
# exists. Consumer species name specific cybernetic property
# bilaterals (@epistemologic/cybernetic/variety, /eigenform, etc.)
# directly in THEIR requires clauses. This adapter exposes the
# integration-altitude check; the per-property checks fire at the
# property altitude.
#
# The signature takes smarts and perturbation as typed parameters per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
#
# Consumer species name this predicate when their operation requires
# @smarts integration-altitude discharge alongside specific
# cybernetic property bilaterals named at consumer altitude.
smarts_satisfies_epistemologic_cybernetic(s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge per substrate-architectural fact ===
#
# This adapter closes the cybernetic_extra-projection altitude of
# "@smarts integrates @epistemologic/cybernetic at substrate altitude":
#  - cybernetic property bundle (bare ref) ↔ smarts.cybernetic_extra
#    round-trips via epistemologic_cybernetic_form_of /
#    epistemologic_cybernetic_as_smarts.
#  - The bilateral discharges @smarts discipline_flexible at
#    integration altitude.
#
# It does NOT discharge any specific cybernetic property at family-
# root altitude (none exists). It does NOT close round-trip identity
# at the smarts-as-whole altitude.
#
# Honest claim post-adapter:
#  - "@smarts integrates @epistemologic/cybernetic at
#    cybernetic_extra-projection altitude" — CLOSED.
#  - "@smarts integrates @epistemologic/cybernetic at family-root
#    bilateral altitude" — STRUCTURALLY-UNAVAILABLE (no family-root
#    bilateral; consumer species name specific property bilaterals).
#  - "@smarts integrates @epistemologic/cybernetic at smarts-as-whole
#    altitude" — FORWARD-PROMISED.

out @smarts/epistemologic
out epistemologic_cybernetic_form_of
out epistemologic_cybernetic_as_smarts
out smarts_satisfies_epistemologic_cybernetic
